							"description": "\n**Consumables**. Your companion can’t use every consumable, but with your help, they can benefit from an edible or drinkable consumable, such as a kolto stim or a ration. While using a kit, your companion can also benefit from a consumable that enhances a weapon, such as a Phase Disruptor Shard. When you use one of these kinds of consumables while you are adjacent to your companion, you can grant the benefit to your companion instead of yourself. You must take the action type required to use the consumable; no action is required of your companion.\n\n**Trinkets**. Your companion can’t use trinkets that are designed to be worn by bipeds (such as cloaks, masks, and hats) or require words or gestures to activate. However, your companion can benefit from one necklace, pendant, collar, or other trinket with the Neck keyword that doesn’t require any action to activate, such as a collar-mounted trinket. You companion doesn’t need to wear their trinket around their neck: a skyslasher might wear a necklace wrapped around a talon, and a dianoga might carry it suspended inside their body!\n\n**Leveled Items**. Although your companion can’t wield a blade, they can benefit from a lightsaber or other master-crafted blade! When you wield and gain the benefits of a leveled weapon, armor, implement, or other item, your companion gains those same benefits as if they were wielding the treasure.",
